{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"edits\":[{\"path\":\"summary/text\",\"value_json\":\"问 means “ask” or “inquire” and is the standardized simplified form of 問. The received analysis of 問 assigns 口 a meaning role and 門 a sound role; the available comparisons do not independently establish the historical sound link.\"},{\"path\":\"summary/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref003\\\",\\\"ref008\\\",\\\"ref019\\\",\\\"ref036\\\",\\\"ref040\\\",\\\"ref051\\\",\\\"ref057\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"formation/text\",\"value_json\":\"The received analysis treats traditional 問 as phonosemantic: 口 supplies a speech-related meaning, while 門 is assigned the sound role. Modern and reconstructed readings can be compared, but do not independently establish the historical correspondence. In 问, 門 is written 门 as part of the simplified form.\"},{\"path\":\"formation/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref003\\\",\\\"ref008\\\",\\\"ref019\\\",\\\"ref036\\\",\\\"ref040\\\",\\\"ref051\\\",\\\"ref057\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"components/2/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref003\\\",\\\"ref026\\\",\\\"ref052\\\",\\\"ref057\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"components/2/origin_relation\",\"value_json\":\"simplified_form\"},{\"path\":\"relationships/2/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref003\\\",\\\"ref026\\\",\\\"ref052\\\",\\\"ref057\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"history/1/text\",\"value_json\":\"Two Shang graphs combining 門 and 口 were traditionally catalogued as 問. Their identification and descent from the later 問 graph are disputed; one tentative alternative is that they are expanded forms of 啟, but their inscriptional meaning remains unclear. A locally inspected 《字源》 entry likewise says the oracle-bone form's meaning was unclear and distinguishes it from later uses.\"},{\"path\":\"history/1/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref017\\\",\\\"ref018\\\",\\\"ref030\\\",\\\"ref051\\\",\\\"ref054\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"meaning_history/senses/0/period\",\"value_json\":\"Late Warring States, as reported for the earliest clear graph in the surveyed evidence\"},{\"path\":\"meaning_history/senses/0/certainty\",\"value_json\":\"established\"},{\"path\":\"meaning_history/senses/0/status\",\"value_json\":\"earliest_attested\"},{\"path\":\"meaning_history/senses/0/text\",\"value_json\":\"The ask/inquire use is reported for late Warring States Qin slips. The received Shuowen gloss 訊 and 《字源》’s gloss “ask/inquire” support this meaning; neither by itself establishes its priority as the original meaning.\"},{\"path\":\"meaning_history/senses/0/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref008\\\",\\\"ref019\\\",\\\"ref029\\\",\\\"ref051\\\",\\\"ref054\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"meaning_history/senses/2/text\",\"value_json\":\"Present-day definitions include “ask about” and “inquire after.”\"},{\"path\":\"meaning_history/senses/2/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref004\\\",\\\"ref011\\\",\\\"ref056\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"meaning_history/limitations/0/text\",\"value_json\":\"The late Warring States dating and Qin-slip examples are reported through scholarly discussion; the cited primary slip records were not checked here.\"},{\"path\":\"meaning_history/limitations/0/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref029\\\",\\\"ref054\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"learner/overview/text\",\"value_json\":\"问 means “ask” or “inquire” and is the simplified form of 問. In the received analysis of 問, 口 contributes meaning and 門 is assigned a sound role, though the available readings do not demonstrate that historical link.\"},{\"path\":\"learner/overview/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref003\\\",\\\"ref008\\\",\\\"ref019\\\",\\\"ref036\\\",\\\"ref040\\\",\\\"ref051\\\",\\\"ref057\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"learner/components/2/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref003\\\",\\\"ref026\\\",\\\"ref052\\\",\\\"ref057\\\"]\"}]}"}}
